    "heading": "Warming Up With a Sweet Easy Win",
    "body": "Happy Saturday, friends! I hope you have a warm mug of something delicious while you look at today's Pips board. The easy puzzle today felt like a gentle breeze. I started by looking at the very bottom left corner where there is a single cell at 3,0 that has to add up to exactly 2. Since that cell is part of a horizontal domino at 3,0 and 3,1, I knew that half of the domino had to be a 2. Looking at our list, the 2,2 domino fits perfectly there, which also helped satisfy the equals constraint for the cell right above it at 2,1.\n\nOnce I had that bottom corner anchored, the rest of the pieces started falling into place like a trail of breadcrumbs. I noticed the constraint at the top left at 0,0 needed a value less than 2, so I tried using the 0,3 domino there. That put a 3 in cell 1,0, which worked perfectly with the equals rule connecting it to 2,0. It is always so satisfying when the numbers just click together without having to overthink it! I finished up by placing the 4,4 and 3,2 dominoes in the remaining spots, making sure all those equals regions were happy.",
