  "tips": "Try looking for the smallest sum regions first because they really limit which dominoes you can use. If you see a large equals region covering four or five cells, remember that every domino touching that area must have that same number on one of its sides. Don't be afraid to pull a domino back off the board if things stop making sense, sometimes a fresh start on a corner is all you need.",
  "learned": "Today I really noticed how important the empty cells are. They act as barriers that dictate which direction your dominoes have to face. In the hard puzzle, the empty cell at 2,3 was the only reason I figured out the orientation of the middle pieces. I also realized that sum constraints with high numbers like 12 are actually your best friends because there is usually only one possible combination of dots that can make them work.",
